{
  "_comment": "Names -> meaning, from scripture. The LIST of names is baked by build-names.mjs into names-index.json (every person of scripture the corpus names often enough, every king); this file only WRITES ABOUT a name: keyed by its Strong's number (sn), `english` = the name translators wrote (shown large on the card; default: the English the reading text gives the name), `origin` = the verse(s) where scripture says why the name was given, `marks` = the words of that verse to light up and the part of each that carries the meaning (prefixes stay unlit), and optionally letters/summary/common/differences/compare/related for the full page. A name not written about here shows the verse it is first named in. Verse text is never copied: /api/names and /api/name/:slug cut each verse from the reader's live text. A new sn here needs `node build-names.mjs` once (to count it).",
  "intro": "A Hebrew name is a sentence. Scripture often says why a name was given, and the reason is spoken in the same root as the name. When a translator replaces the name with one that neither looks nor sounds like it, the reason in the verse goes silent. Each name here is shown in its own letters, with the verse that explains it, beside the names translators chose.",
